;">FOFANA=E2=80=99S PENALTY GOES POSTAL</h2></div></td></tr>
<tr><td align=3D"left" class=3D"text" style=3D"background:#FFFFFF;font-size=
:0px;padding:0 16px;word-break:break-word;"><div style=3D"font-family:Georg=
ia, serif;font-size:16px;font-weight:400;line-height:22px;text-align:left;c=
olor:#121212;">
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Football Daily isn=E2=80=99t suggesting st=
andards at Chelsea have slipped in recent years, but the quality of their p=
layers who miss penalties in shootouts against Liverpool certainly appears =
to be on the slide. Before last night, footballing royalty such as Arjen Ro=
bben, Geremi, Tammy Abraham, C=C3=A9sar Azpilicueta, Mason Mount and even g=
oalkeeper Kepa Arrizabalaga had all missed from the spot in four consecutiv=
e post-match deciders against Liverpool across 19 years and four different =
competitions. On Wednesday, a flame-haired Argentinian irritant, a striker =
we=E2=80=99d never previously heard of before yesterday and a defensive lia=
bility whose boots increasingly look to have been welded on to the wrong fe=
et each added their names to the roll of shame. Valent=C3=ADn Barco, Emanue=
l Emegha and Wesley Fofana, take a collective bow.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">On a night when the two head coaches made =
a combined 11 changes to their starting lineups, it was Liverpool who advan=
ced to the Fizzy Cup quarter-finals. Any remaining doubt that Liverpool wou=
ld notch up yet another shootout win over Chelsea evaporated when Fofana=E2=
=80=99s penalty proved more of a threat to the windscreens of passing motor=
ists on nearby Walton Breck Road than Giorgi Mamardashvili=E2=80=99s goal. =
=E2=80=9CThis is football, this is part of our job,=E2=80=9D sighed Xabi Al=
onso, over the sound of screeching brakes and shattering glass. =E2=80=9CWe=
 played with courage, the game was close with not many chances for both sid=
es. It is a small setback because it is probably the least important compet=
ition for us.=E2=80=9D Despite Alonso=E2=80=99s assessment of Fizzy Cup=E2=
=80=99s place in the domestic trophy pecking order being entirely correct, =
he has been accused of being disrespectful towards a competition that has p=
reviously staged its first round draw in a Morrisons supermarket and once s=
eriously harboured notions of conducting a zero-gravity equivalent in outer=
 space.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">The Chelsea head coach is also accused of =
contemptuousness towards Est=C3=AAv=C3=A3o, the young Brazilian tyro consid=
ered a certainty to start in the absence of Cole Palmer, but spent the even=
ing looking increasingly forlorn on the bench. Despite repeated calls for t=
he introduction of =E2=80=9CSteve-oh!=E2=80=9D from travelling Chelsea fans=
, Alonso elected not to use the 19-year-old, prompting rumours of some sort=
 of rift. =E2=80=9CI understand his situation and that he could be happier =
for sure,=E2=80=9D he parped of a future superstar who has spent just 172 m=
inutes on the pitch under his watch. =E2=80=9CWe have had some intense game=
s and there will be moments for everything. I=E2=80=99m sure Est=C3=AA will=
 have his moment.=E2=80=9D</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">As for Liverpool, progressing felt less li=
ke a triumph of tactical ingenuity and more like an unavoidable civic duty,=
 on a par with renewing one=E2=80=99s car tax or desperately trying to get =
out of jury service. Their reward is a quarter-final tie at home to Bournem=
outh, setting up a potentially awkward reunion between Andoni Iraola and th=
e club he left behind for bigger things. =E2=80=9CHonestly, I was talking b=
efore the draw and I said: =E2=80=98The only team I don=E2=80=99t want is B=
ournemouth=E2=80=99,=E2=80=9D he sighed. =E2=80=9CFor me, it=E2=80=99s spec=
ial. They know me very well. They are playing very well lately, in a good m=
oment but it is what it is.=E2=80=9D On the bright side, with this being th=
e lowly Fizzy Cup, he won=E2=80=99t have to pretend to be too upset when on=
e of the two sides competing on four different fronts inevitably gets knock=
ed out.</p>
